# EFEX Trivy Ignore File - Baselined Vulnerabilities
# ===================================================
# These vulnerabilities have been reviewed and accepted due to:
# - No fix available from upstream
# - Bundled dependencies (e.g., OpenSSL in cryptography wheel)
# - Low exploitability in our context
#
# Last reviewed: 2026-08-02
# Reviewed by: Platform Security Team

# Cryptography package bundled OpenSSL vulnerabilities
# These are in pre-built wheels and require upstream fix
# Reference: GHSA-537c-gmf6-5ccf
CVE-2026-34073
CVE-2026-39892
CVE-2026-26007

# MySQL Connector known issues in bundled OpenSSL
# Awaiting upstream fix in next release
# Reference: https://dev.mysql.com/doc/relnotes/connector-python/en/

# pyasn1 vulnerabilities - pinned by python-jose dependency (requires pyasn1<0.5.0)
# These are in a transitive dependency with version constraints we cannot override
# Risk accepted: JOSE token parsing is server-side only, no untrusted ASN.1 input
# Reference: https://github.com/mpdavis/python-jose/issues/375
CVE-2026-23490
CVE-2026-30922
CVE-2026-59884
CVE-2026-59885
CVE-2026-59886

# jaraco.context vulnerability - transitive dependency of setuptools
# Path traversal requires malicious tar archive processing (not in our use case)
# Reference: GHSA-58pv-8j8x-9vj2
CVE-2026-23949

# Base image (python:3.11-slim-bookworm) pip, setuptools, and wheel
# These are in the system Python, not in our virtualenv
# Our app uses pip==26.1.2, setuptools==83.0.0, wheel>=0.46.2 in /opt/venv
CVE-2025-8869
CVE-2026-1703
CVE-2026-3219
CVE-2026-6357
CVE-2026-8643
CVE-2026-59890
CVE-2026-24049
